# Speckit Implementation Plan

## Purpose

This plan describes how to build the beginner-friendly Django personal banking app defined in the constitution, specification, clarifications, and checklist.

## Technical Direction

- Python 3.11 or later
- Django
- SQLite3 for local development
- Django templates for page rendering
- pytest, pytest-django, and pytest-cov for tests and coverage
- SonarQube or SonarCloud for code quality analysis
- GitHub Actions for CI
- Waitress for simple Windows local deployment

## Planning Principles

- Keep the code readable for workshop learners.
- Use standard Django structure before adding extra abstraction.
- Keep business rules visible in models, forms, views, and tests.
- Prefer one obvious implementation path over configurable complexity.

## Architecture Overview

The MVP will use a single Django project with one main app that contains the banking workflow.

- Project package responsibility:
  - settings
  - root URL configuration
  - WSGI entry point for Waitress
- Banking app responsibility:
  - account registration
  - account detail display
  - deposit and withdrawal flows
  - transaction history
  - domain validation in forms and model methods

This keeps the implementation easy to teach and trace in a workshop.

